						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16549#msg16549">Quote from: Bobo on April 19, 2005, 04:11:15 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">We just had honest people who always reported what had been done,</div>  <br />Maybe while you were at the helm</div>Couldn&#039;t comment on that since I have only hearsay about what happened afterwards.<br />Either way I had made it obvious that I&#039;d rip anyone another asshole if I spied Qvic gear on them that wasn&#039;t in our dkp. It would cost 10 times what<br />the item would have cost with the guild. Rather easier to just report the raid, pay the pretty low price and even gain dkp if you didn&#039;t take anything.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">And you don&#039;t need MQ to get to them quickly unless you&#039;re really stupid and inept. ESPECIALLY not if you had level 70 when you went for them</div>  <br />Of course not rogue &amp; Cleric hammer worked fine, Watched  .........  do it many times right in front of us.</div>We never really needed that either. Not like those mobs had a lot of hitpoints. We just CoHd to the middle and slaughtered our way to them (and<br />then had a good bard pull when the way was somewhat clear). Never took particularly long.</td>
