							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1512.msg16302#msg16302">Quote from: Lhyra on April 08, 2005, 12:49:51 pm</a></div><div class="quote">The worst thing that can happen in the game is to lose experience when you die.  You can’t even lose your gear anymore.  So when you lose experience, it just means you play more (which you should be enjoying) to get it back.</div>We spent roughly 40 hours in Uqua before DA/EiE even zoned in there or FoTime/Conviction found the zone. Then we spent roughly 100h more with the peak of our development being killing _4_ mobs in a single run! (holy fucking shit) We might have been the ONLY guild that got that initial trap down during Uquas original state of insane AEs and totally crazy melee (the AEs were like 3k from the adds? Meleed for 4000 or so). That took us 140 hours.<br /><br />We died every chance we got, so dunno how often corpses popped out. Guess we died 140 times each with roughly 50 people to get 4 mobs down (we got few of the trap mobs down before, so probably like 20 is a more realistic number). Considering on average we had like 500 mobs deaths per 1 member death, this new ratio of 7000 member deaths to 20 mob deaths was pretty goddamn annoying.<br /><br />I can also assure you nobody felt like playing the game to regain experience (which was a non-issue anyway) after all that wasted time.<br /><br />Some end game bugginess is to be expected (we wasted quite a bit of time on a bugged Onyxia in WoW for example), but Uqua in GoD was just fucking EXTREME. Oh and making sure everyone got all 3 trials done was bit of a PITA... and then people didn&#039;t even need it anymore.</td>
